{{Icelandic declension kk sb maður|}}
===Etymology===
Old Norse ''[[maðr]]''
===Noun===
'''maður''' {{m}}

# [[man]], [[human being]]
#* ''[[það|Það]] [[tilheyra|tilheyrir]] [[náttúra|náttúru]] '''mannsins''' [[hata|að hata]] [[þeir|þá]] [[sem]] [[hann]] [[hafa|hefur]] [[særa|sært]].''
#*: It belongs to '''human''' [[nature]] [[hate|to hate]] those that he has [[injure]]d.
# [[husband]] (most often used with {{def}} article)
#* ''[[þetta|Þetta]] er '''maðurinn''' [[minn]] Geir.''
#*: This is [[my]] '''husband''', Geir. 
# [[chessman]]
#* ''[[færa|Færðu]] '''manninn''' [[þinn]].''
#*: [[move|Move]] [[your]] '''chessman'''.

